-- Tests for au-time-rules.l4.
-- This file sits beside the module because an IMPORT searches only the importing file's own folder.
-- Every expected value below is the value the SOURCE module for that jurisdiction printed for the same input;
-- the differential report (au-time-rules.differential.md) records how the inputs were chosen and the counts.
-- Each shared function has at least three assertions for every jurisdiction in its table row, drawn from the probe grid so that
-- month ends, 29 February, year ends, a Sunday and a holiday input are covered where the function can be asked about them.
-- A jurisdiction that does not encode a function is asserted to answer NOTHING.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-time-rules`


§ `F01 does a period expressed this way include the specified day`

-- Cth
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Cth `between two days`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Cth `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Cth `ends before a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Cth `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Cth `is reckoned to a specified day`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- NSW
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NSW `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NSW `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NSW `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NSW `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- Vic
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Vic `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Vic `ends before a specified day`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Vic `is reckoned to a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Vic `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Vic `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- Qld
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Qld `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Qld `begins at, on or with a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Qld `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Qld `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Qld `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- WA
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` WA `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` WA `continues until a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` WA `ends before a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` WA `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` WA `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- SA
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` SA `between two days`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` SA `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` SA `ends before a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` SA `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` SA `is reckoned to a specified day`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- Tas
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Tas `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Tas `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Tas `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` Tas `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- ACT
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` ACT `occurs between two events`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` ACT `continues until a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` ACT `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` ACT `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` ACT `is reckoned to a specified day`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
-- NT
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NT `between two days`) EQUALS (NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NT `begins from a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` NT `ends at, on or with a specified day`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)

